\begin{abstract}
% Transformer-based models have demonstrated superior performance in various fields, including natural language processing and computer vision. However, the growing size of these models, along with their increased computational, memory, and communication demands, limits their feasibility to large-scale servers --- even for inference only. Binary transformers offer a promising solution for edge deployment, thanks to their compact model size, low computational complexity, reduced communication bandwidth requirement, and acceptable inference accuracy. However, current binary transformer approaches cannot be directly deployed on existing hardware due to the absence of optimized binary matrix multiplication execution units, leading to suboptimal performance. To unlock the full potential of binary transformers, we propose \textbf{COD-BT}, an Algorithm-Architecture co-designed Binary Transformer Accelerator optimized for edge computing. We propose an efficient real 1-bit binary multiplication unit, enabling matrix multiplication for matrices with -1, 0, and +1 values, unlike existing ternary approaches. Along with several other innovations and hardware-friendly optimizations in the attention block, COD-BT achieves up to 3894.7 GOPS throughput and 448.7 GOPS/W energy efficiency on edge FPGAs, delivering a 300× improvement over GPUs and a 3.5× enhancement over state-of-the-art binary accelerators, with negligible accuracy trade-offs.

Transformer-based models have demonstrated superior performance in various fields, including natural language processing and computer vision. However, their enormous model size and high demands in computation, memory, and communication limit their deployment to edge platforms for local, secure inference. Binary transformers offer a compact, low-complexity solution for edge deployment with reduced bandwidth needs and acceptable accuracy. Yet, existing binary transformers underperform on current hardware due to the lack of optimized binary matrix multiplication units. To address this, we introduce COD-BT, an algorithm-architecture co-optimized binary Transformer accelerator for edge computing. COD-BT features a real 1-bit binary multiplication unit, enabling matrix operations with -1, 0, and +1 values, surpassing ternary methods. With further hardware-friendly optimizations in the attention block, COD-BT achieves up to 3894.7 GOPS throughput and 448.7 GOPS/W energy efficiency on edge FPGAs, delivering a 311× energy efficiency improvement over GPUs and a 3.5× throughput improvement over the state-of-the-art binary accelerator, with only negligible accuracy degradation.

\end{abstract}

