To overcome these limitations, we propose \textbf{COD-BT}, a hardware/software co-designed Binary Transformer Accelerator optimized for edge FPGAs. COD-BT introduces several innovations, including the \textit{Shifted Polarized Softmax (SPS)} for hardware-efficient attention, a true 1-bit binary multiplication method for \(-1\), \(0\), and \(+1\) matrices, and integer packing to maximize bandwidth. Additional optimizations, such as efficient popcount units, operation fusion, processing element reuse, and parallelism tuning, enhance throughput, latency, and resource utilization. Our evaluations show that COD-BT operates efficiently on both mid-range edge FPGA (ZCU102) and low-power edge FPGA (KV260), making it robust for resource-limited edge deployment.
