      \field{abstract}{This report provides background analysis for debate about a research system in transition. Plan S, launched by Science Europe on 4 September 2018, is intended to increase Open Access (OA) to research data and reports produced through publicly-funded academic research. OA is expected to enable and accelerate discovery and innovation. Plan S requires research funded by signatory organisations to be published in open repositories or in journals where all papers are publicly accessible. This report looks at recent patterns of papers funded by Plan S supporters using perspectives related to funders, subjects, countries, publishers, and journals. It focuses on analysis and variances rather than scenarios.}
