For the evaluation of our system, we use the Sample100 dataset \cite{vanbalen_2011}
%, the only publicly available collection of annotations specifically addressing samples in ``real-world'' commercially released music %
. The dataset consists of 75 full-length hip-hop recordings (queries) containing samples from 68 full-length songs (references) across a variety of genres, with R\&B/Soul representing the majority \cite{cheston_2025}. It contains 106 sample relationships and a total of 137 sample occurrences, as some queries use multiple samples and some references appear in multiple queries. To challenge retrieval systems, the dataset includes 320 additional ``noise'' tracks with a similar genre distribution, which are not sampled in any query. %, bringing the total candidate pool to 388 tracks.

