only a small portion of each candidate track is sampled and present in queries - sample lengths range from just one second to 26 seconds. The samples represent real-world musical ``transformative appropriation'' \cite{demers_2006}, including both tonal (\textit{riffs}), percussive drum break (\textit{beats}), and \textit{1-note} micro-samples. %The initial intention of \cite{vanbalen_2011} was that all samples would be direct uses of audio from the original recordings (not interpolations/re-recordings), but the public annotations include a label indicating possible interpolation in some of the samples. 
