\section{Derived rules}
\label{appendix:derived_rules}

We show an example derivation for the rules of polarized exponentials with polarities, in this case $\forall^+$ and $\exists^\Delta$:
  \[
  \begin{prooftree}
  \hypo{\Delta,\Gamma \vdash \rho : P}
  \hypo{[\Theta \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma]\ \Phi \vdash \forall^+ x.\psi(x)}
  \infer2[\Ruleforall]{[\Theta \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma,x:P]\ \Phi \vdash \psi(x)}
  \infer1[\Rulereindex]{[\Theta \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma]\ \Phi \vdash \psi(\rho)}
  \end{prooftree}
  \]
  To establish the $\exists^\Delta$ rule, we first start with the following derivation:
  \[
\begin{prooftree}
\hypo{\Delta \vdash \delta : D}
\infer1[\Rulehyp]{[\Theta \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma]\ \exists^\Delta x.\psi(\n x,x),\Phi \vdash \exists^\Delta x.\psi(\n x,x)}
\infer1[\Ruleexists]{[\Theta \mid \Delta,x:D \mid \Gamma]\ \psi(\n x,x),\Phi \vdash \exists^\Delta x.\psi(\n x,x)}
\infer1[\Rulereindex]{[\Theta \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma]\ \psi(\delta,\delta),\Phi \vdash \exists^\Delta x.\psi(\n x,x)}
\end{prooftree}
\]
and then one can derive the $\exists^\Delta$ rule by applying $\Rulecut$ with a generic propositional context on the left.

We show that the $\Uparrow$ direction of $\Rulele$ implies reflexivity of directed equality: take the rule
\[
\begin{prooftree}
\hypo{[\Theta,a:A \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma,b:A]\ {a \le b,\Phi} & \vdash \varphi(a,b)}
\infer1[\Rulele]{[\Theta \mid \Delta, z:A \mid \Gamma]\ \takespace{a \le b,\Phi}{\Phi} & \vdash \varphi(\nzz)}
\end{prooftree}
\]
By instantiating it with $\varphi(a,b) := a \le b$,
\[
\begin{prooftree}
\infer0[\Rulehyp]{[\Theta,a:A \mid \Delta \mid \Gamma,b:A]\ {a \le b,\Phi} & \vdash a \le b}
\infer1{[\Theta \mid \Delta, z:A \mid \Gamma]\ \takespace{a \le b,\Phi}{\Phi} & \vdash \n z \le z}
\end{prooftree}
\]
as desired. The rule $\Rulereflterm$ is obtained by $\Rulereindex$ the only dinatural variable in the last derivation with an arbitrary term $\Delta \vdash \delta : A$.

We show additional derived rules in \Cref{fig:syntax:derived_rules_polarized_exponentials,fig:syntax:derived_rules_equality,fig:syntax:derived_rules_quantifiers}.

