\section*{Organization of the appendix}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \Cref{gen-and-Byzantine} contains deferred proofs for~\Cref{II-Background-motivation}, focusing on the link between uniform stability and generalization bounds under Byzantine failure and poisoning attacks.
    \item \Cref{loss-regularities} summarizes the regularity assumptions and includes key expansivity results.
    \item \Cref{robust-section-deferred} formally defines $\mathrm{SMEA}$ and $\mathrm{CWTM}$, along with their key known properties.
    \item \Cref{deferred-sec-3} provides detailed proofs for the stability analysis of robust distributed $\mathrm{GD}$ and $\mathrm{SGD}$ presented in~\Cref{III-main}. This includes: 
    bounds on the expected (trace and spectral) norm of the empirical covariance of the honest gradients'~(\Cref{empirical-cov-expectation-1}), used for bounding uniform stability under Byzantine attacks; 
    upper bounds on uniform stability under Byzantine attacks~(\Cref{stability-analysis-classic-byzantine}), with detailed proofs of~\Cref{byz-sgd-ub-convex,byz-sgd-ub-nonconvex};
    properties of the $\mathrm{CWTM}$ aggregation rule~(\Cref{tm}), used to improve stability bounds under poisoning attacks for smooth nonconvex objectives;
    upper bounds on uniform stability under poisoning attacks with $\mathrm{SMEA}$ and $\mathrm{CWTM}$~(\Cref{stability-poisonous}), corresponding to proofs of~\Cref{th-poisoning-convex-smea-main-text,poi-cwtm-ub};
    and lower bounds on uniform stability under poisoning attacks with $\mathrm{SMEA}$~(\Cref{lb-smea-gd,lb-smea-sgd}), including the proof of~\Cref{lower-bound-gd-poisonous-merged}.
    \item \Cref{deferred-section-4} specifies details supporting~\Cref{V-experimental}, including numerical experiments~(\Cref{appD-numerical-experiment}) and generalization error computations~(\Cref{gen-error-linear}).
    \item \Cref{refined-heterogeneity} gives example of results with refined bounded heterogeneity and bounded variance assumptions instead of the more general bounded gradients assumption.
    \item \Cref{IV-excessrisk} discusses high-probability excess risk bounds for robust distributed learning under smooth and strongly convex loss functions.
\end{itemize}

